    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-20T04:10:25+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T04:10:25+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T17:40:25Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T17:40:25Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system in the Bight will drift southeast as the associated trough crosses eastern South Australia clears before clearing later Friday. A weak high pressure system briefly moves across southern SA later Friday before a trough and cold front then move into the west from Saturday evening and cross the rest of SA on Sunday. A high will then push in behind the front and will move across the Bight early next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW006" description="Riverland" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm during the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds near the eastern border. Winds north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h turning west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the early afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of fog in the west in the early morning. Winds southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light before dawn. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h shifting west to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to the low 20s with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
